              "text": "To watch MSNBC live online, it is helpful to note a major update regarding the network: **MSNBC officially rebranded to MS NOW** (short for *My Source for News, Opinion, and the World*). This change occurred after parent company Comcast spun off its cable channels into a standalone media company called Versant. Despite the new name and logo, the programming, hosts, and shows (such as *Morning Joe*, *The Rachel Maddow Show*, and *The Beat with Ari Melber*) remain the same.\n\nWhile there is **no official, 100% free legal live video stream** of MS NOW (MSNBC) without a subscription, you can still access the channel's live broadcast and daily content for free using the following official and legal methods:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Free Live Audio Streaming (100% Free)\nIf you just want to listen to the live broadcast on your phone or computer, you can stream the audio live for free, 24/7:\n* **TuneIn Radio:** You can stream the live MS NOW audio broadcast for free on the TuneIn website or the TuneIn app. \n* **The MS NOW App:** The official MS NOW app allows users to listen to the live audio stream of the network for free without needing to sign in.\n\n### 2. Free Clips and Full Segments on YouTube (100% Free)\nIf you don't need a continuous live feed but want to watch the latest commentary and breaking news coverage:\n* **Official YouTube Channel:** The official **@msnow** YouTube channel uploads free, high-definition video clips of almost every major segment from shows like *Morning Joe*, *Deadline: White House*, and *The Rachel Maddow Show* shortly after they air. \n\n### 3. Stream Live with a TV Provider Login\nIf you, a family member, or a friend already pay for a traditional cable package, satellite TV, or a live TV streaming service (like YouTube TV or Hulu + Live TV):\n* You can download the **MS NOW app** on your phone, tablet, Roku, Apple TV, or Fire TV.\n* Select **\"Sign In with TV Provider,\"** enter the login credentials, and you will unlock the 24/7 live video stream at no extra cost.\n\n### 4. Use Free Trials on Live TV Streaming Services\nIf you need to watch a specific live event (like election coverage or a special broadcast) for free, you can sign up for a free trial of a digital live TV streaming service. *Just remember to cancel before the trial period ends to avoid being charged.*\n* **DirecTV Stream:** Frequently offers a **5-day free trial** and includes MS NOW in its base \"Entertainment\" package.\n* **Fubo:** Typically offers a **7-day free trial**.\n* **YouTube TV:** Offers varying free trials (usually 7 to 14 days). \n* **Sling TV (Sling Blue):** Does not always have a free trial, but regularly offers heavily discounted first-month promotional rates.\n\n*(Note: Because of the corporate split from NBCUniversal, **Peacock no longer carries MS NOW** content).*\n\n---\n\n*A quick warning regarding \"free live TV\" websites:* There are unofficial, third-party sites on the web that claim to stream MS NOW/MSNBC for free. These streams are legally unauthorized, highly unreliable, and often contain intrusive pop-up ads, malware, or phishing risks. Using the official routes listed above is the safest and highest-quality way to stay updated.",
